 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 508075,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "On June 9, 2021, 1 U.S. dollar was worth 1.21 Canadian dollars. Write this comparison as a ratio.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>There are three ways to write ratios: <i>a</i> to <i>b</i>, <i>a</i>:<i>b</i>, or <i>a</i>/<i>b</i>, which can be written with fraction notation <span data-math=\"\\left( {\\frac{a}{b}} \\right)\"></span>.</p>\n<p>If <span data-math=\"a = 1\"></span> U.S. dollar, and <span data-math=\"b = 1.21\"></span> Canadian dollars, the ratio can be written in one of three ways.</p>\n<p>1 to 1.21</p>\n<p>1:1.21</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\frac{1}{{1.21}}\"></span></p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"a\">a</span> = 1 U.S. dollar, and <span data-math=\"b\">b</span> = 1.21 Canadian dollars, the ratio is 1 to 1.21; or 1:1.21; or <span data-math=\"\\frac{1}{{1.21}}\">\\frac{1}{{1.21}}</span> ."
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
